Comon (1994) observed that the Darmois–Skitovich theorem settles the identifiability of ICA. The argument works directly with the global matrix $ P =  W A$, which maps the sources to the outputs, $ y =  P s$. Comon（1994）注意到，Darmois–Skitovich 定理解决了 ICA 的可辨识性问题。论证直接针对把源映射到输出的全局矩阵 $ P =  W A$ 进行，即 $ y =  P s$。 What the theorem is checking. $ P= W A$ describes the full trip from true sources to estimated outputs. An invertible $ P$ has not compressed away a source dimension. The theorem assumes exact pairwise independence of its outputs—not small sample correlations—and concludes that each output uses exactly one source. The proof explains why a non-Gaussian source cannot be shared between two independent outputs. 定理究竟在检查什么？ $ P= W A$ 描述从真实源到估计输出的完整过程。$ P$ 可逆表示没有压掉任何一个源维度。定理假设输出严格两两独立，而不是样本相关很小；结论是每个输出恰好使用一个源。证明解释了为什么两个独立输出不能共享一个非高斯源。 Let $ s = (s_1, \dots, s_n)^	op$ have mutually independent, non-degenerate components with finite variances, at most one of which is Gaussian, and let $ P \in \R^{n 	imes n}$ be invertible. If the components of $ y =  P s$ are pairwise independent, then $ P =  Pi D$ for some permutation matrix $ Pi$ and invertible diagonal matrix $ D$. In particular, the components of $ y$ are then mutually independent. 设 $ s = (s_1, \dots, s_n)^	op$ 的各分量相互独立、非退化且方差有限，其中至多一个是高斯的；设 $ P \in \R^{n 	imes n}$ 可逆。若 $ y =  P s$ 的各分量两两独立，则存在置换矩阵 $ Pi$ 与可逆对角矩阵 $ D$，使 $ P =  Pi D$。特别地，此时 $ y$ 的各分量相互独立。 Take two rows $i 
