eq 0$ is Gaussian. Hence each column $k$ that belongs to a non-Gaussian source has at most one nonzero entry, and at least one because $ P$ is invertible. These columns are multiples of standard basis vectors and are linearly independent, so their nonzero entries lie in distinct rows. If no source is Gaussian, this already says $ P =  Pi D$. 任取两行 $i 
