eq 0$ because $ P$ is invertible. Any other row $i$ has the form $y_i = P_{il} s_l + P_{ig} s_g$, where $l$ is the non-Gaussian column whose nonzero entry sits in row $i$. Independent variables with finite variance are uncorrelated, so $0 = \Cov(y_i, y_r) = P_{ig} P_{rg} \Var(s_g)$, which forces $P_{ig} = 0$. Thus column $g$ also has a single nonzero entry, and $ P =  Pi D$. Finally, $ Pi D s$ has mutually independent components ( ). 否则，设 $s_g$ 是那个高斯源。$n - 1$ 个非高斯列占据了 $n - 1$ 个不同的行，记剩下的一行为 $r$。第 $r$ 行在第 $g$ 列以外全为零，所以 $y_r = P_{rg} s_g$；又因 $ P$ 可逆，$P_{rg} 
eq 0$。其余任一行 $i$ 都形如 $y_i = P_{il} s_l + P_{ig} s_g$，其中 $l$ 是非零元恰在第 $i$ 行的那个非高斯列。方差有限的独立变量互不相关，故 $0 = \Cov(y_i, y_r) = P_{ig} P_{rg} \Var(s_g)$，这迫使 $P_{ig} = 0$。于是第 $g$ 列也只有一个非零元，即 $ P =  Pi D$。最后，$ Pi D s$ 的各分量相互独立（ ）。 The Gaussian column needs the separate covariance step because the Darmois–Skitovich theorem places no restriction on a Gaussian variable shared by two forms. Applied to the ICA model, the theorem gives identifiability. 高斯列之所以需要单独的协方差论证，是因为 Darmois–Skitovich 定理对两个线性形式共享的高斯变量没有任何限制。把这个定理用到 ICA 模型上，就得到可辨识性。 Let $ x =  A s$ satisfy , with non-degenerate sources of finite variance. If $ W \in \R^{n 	imes m}$ makes $ W A$ invertible and the components of $ y =  W x$ pairwise independent, then $ W A =  Pi D$: the outputs are the sources up to order and scale. The mixing matrix is identifiable: if $ A s \overset{d}{=}  B t$ where $( B,  t)$ also satisfies these assumptions, then $ B =  A Pi D$. 设 $ x =  A s$ 满足 ，且各源非退化、方差有限。 若 $ W \in \R^{n 	imes m}$ 使 $ W A$ 可逆，并使 $ y =  W x$ 的各分量两两独立，则 $ W A =  Pi D$：输出就是在顺序与尺度意义下的源。 混合矩阵可辨识：若 $ A s \overset{d}{=}  B t$，且 $( B,  t)$ 也满足上述假设，则 $ B =  A Pi D$。 Part 1 is applied to $ P =  W A$. For part 2, the covariance of $ x$ is $ A Sigma_{ s} A^	op =  B Sigma_{ t} B^	op$ with positive definite diagonal $ Sigma_{ s}$ and $ Sigma_{ t}$, so $ A$ and $ B$ have the same column space. Let $ A^{+}$ be the pseudo-inverse, so that $ A^{+} A =  I$ and $ A A^{+}$ is the orthogonal projector onto that column space; then $ A M =  B$ for $ M =  A^{+} B$, and $ M$ is invertible because $ B$ has rank $n$. Applying $ A^{+}$ to both sides of $ A s \overset{d}{=}  B t$ gives $ s \overset{d}{=}  M t$, so $ M t$ has mutually independent components. By applied to $ t$, $ M =  Pi D$, and $ B =  A Pi D$. 第 1 条就是把 用于 $ P =  W A$。对第 2 条，$ x$ 的协方差为 $ A Sigma_{ s} A^	op =  B Sigma_{ t} B^	op$，其中 $ Sigma_{ s}$ 与 $ Sigma_{ t}$ 是正定对角矩阵，所以 $ A$ 与 $ B$ 的列空间相同。记 $ A^{+}$ 为伪逆，则 $ A^{+} A =  I$，且 $ A A^{+}$ 是到该列空间的正交投影；于是对 $ M =  A^{+} B$ 有 $ A M =  B$，又因 $ B$ 的秩为 $n$，$ M$ 可逆。对 $ A s \overset{d}{=}  B t$ 两边作用 $ A^{+}$，得 $ s \overset{d}{=}  M t$，所以 $ M t$ 的各分量相互独立。对 $ t$ 应用 ，得 $ M =  Pi D$，从而 $ B =  A Pi D$。 Two features of deserve emphasis. First, pairwise independence of the outputs is enough. For general random vectors pairwise independence is much weaker than mutual independence ( ), but for invertible linear transforms of independent sources the two coincide. It is therefore enough, in principle, to make the outputs independent pair by pair. The algorithm of Comon (1994) is built on this: it sweeps repeatedly over the pairs of outputs, rotating each pair to optimize a contrast, and JADE uses the same pairwise Jacobi sweeps ( ). Second, the theorem justifies the notion of a contrast function (Comon, 1994): any criterion that is optimized only when the outputs are independent is optimized only at separating matrices. The mutual information of the outputs in is the canonical example. 有两点值得强调。第一，输出 两两 独立就足够了。对一般的随机向量，两两独立远弱于相互独立（ ）；但对独立源的可逆线性变换，两者是一回事。因此，原则上只需让输出两两独立即可。Comon（1994）的算法正是建立在这一点之上：它反复扫描各对输出，每次旋转一对输出以优化对比函数；JADE 也采用同样的成对 Jacobi 扫描（ ）。第二，该定理为 对比函数 的概念提供了依据（Comon, 1994）：凡是只在输出独立时才取到最优的准则，都只在分离矩阵处取到最优。 中输出的互信息就是最典型的例子。
